From 4ae6a9edfe63e0675c55b63c9fadbf1d960ae623 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:28:25 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(app,ui): built-in parametric milling vises in the
 fixture library
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A generic vise (3, 4, 5, 6, 8 in; 100, 125, 150, 160, 200 mm jaw widths)
is generated geometry: its side profile (base, fixed jaw, moving jaw at
the opening, screw and handle housing) extruded across the body width,
one closed outward shell. It is placed through the fixture library's
InsertFixture path (InsertVise), so it is an ordinary meshed fixture to
the collision laws; its parameters ride the FixtureDef marker (and the
project file's optional fixture `vise` key), so SetVise regenerates it
at a new jaw opening or size in one undo unit. The opening can be set
from the setup's stock: fitted on placement (fixed jaw on the stock's
+Y side, centred, floor under it) or re-opened as the vise stands.
Nonsense parameters are refused by name.

UI: "Add built-in vise…" on the Fixtures node menu and page; a vise
row edits its jaw opening (Set opening, Open to stock). MCP:
add_builtin_vise and set_vise.

Fixes #788

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
