From 9d8c7fa1da55a5191d7a4829d982ce88fcd106ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:42:10 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat(app,ui): built-in workholding accessories in the
 fixture library
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Parallels (a pair, with an optional fit under the stock inside a built-in
vise: the height set so the stock top stands a stated amount over the
jaws, the vise dropped to suit, one undo unit), 1-2-3 blocks, step
blocks, strap (toe) clamps (strap, stud, heel block, clamp height) and
soft jaws, each generated from a few dimensions as closed shells that
touch but never overlap. Placed through InsertFixture (InsertAccessory)
and resized through UpdateModel (SetAccessory), so the existing fixture
mesh laws judge them; the parameters ride the FixtureDef marker and the
project file's optional fixture `accessory` key. Nonsense is refused by
name.

UI: "Add accessory…" on the Fixtures node menu and page (the fixture
library's modal); each accessory row keeps its own size draft and
applies it with one SetAccessory. MCP: add_accessory, set_accessory.

Fixes #789

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
